{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "recorded": "2026-09-12T02:00:00-04:00",
  "status": "applied; jar copies pending release",
  "description": "Restore stripe-matched awning stairs on every market template. Each eave stair takes the stair the original market set used for the stripe colour above it, so the awning stripes continue down the eaves instead of stopping at one family-wide stair type.",
  "mapping": {
    "white": "minecraft:birch_stairs",
    "red": "minecraft:mangrove_stairs",
    "cyan": "minecraft:warped_stairs",
    "orange": "minecraft:acacia_stairs",
    "green": "minecraft:mossy_cobblestone_stairs",
    "yellow": "minecraft:bamboo_stairs"
  },
  "precedent": "The original Plains, Savanna, Taiga and Snowy markets (removed from the jar in 2a55bb2, \"Remove the old Village Life catalogs\") used birch under white, mangrove under red, warped under cyan and acacia under orange. Green and yellow stripes only exist in the Desert and Floodplain markets and had no original stair; they take the mossy cobblestone and bamboo stairs Aaron chose on the Mediterranean workshop tier 3.",
  "defect": "Every regional restyle mapped all awning stairs to one family stair (smooth sandstone, smooth red sandstone, mud brick, jungle, spruce); Birch kept only the warped stairs under cyan. Decision: Aaron, 2026-09-12, \"do what the original set had\".",
  "stripe_rule": "A stair is an awning stair when a wool, terracotta or concrete block touches it, checked behind its high side first, then above, then beside; every stair in these templates qualifies.",
  "tool": "tools/structure/ReplaceTemplateBlocks.java (typed NbtIo read and write; swaps the named cells to the new block keeping facing, half and shape; drops palette entries nothing uses any more, which is why the datapack palettes shrink)",
  "plan": "run/market-stripe-repair-20260912/plan.json (restripe.py plans and audits; before.json and after.json hold the hashes)",
